{
 "_note": "WI-057 design (revised 2026-09-13 after the fresh review, F3/N1): the physical owner proposed for every EXISTING attribute -- the 199 the generic MFE plant declares (mfe_plant.sysml@3d7b446c), the Stellaris instance's own 6, the magnet definition's 31 and the 15 the costed subsystem definitions declare (unit_cost, cost_per_mw etc. listed once per owner). Inherited costed-component attributes (capital_cost, cas_code, account_name, scope) are unchanged and not listed. New EXPOSE attributes are listed in design.md D5, not here. Key = attribute name (names never change; only the owner path does). Value = new owner path relative to the plant, or 'plant:<reason class>' for a quantity that stays on the plant.",
 "_reasons": {
  "plant:economics": "financial rates, cost rollups, CAS aggregations, levelized annual costs, the LCOE chain",
  "plant:power-balance": "the plant-level electrical balance and its exposed powers",
  "plant:lifecycle": "the lifecycle calendar's own inputs and outputs: availability, the outage length, the unplanned fraction, the replacement cost; a component's own life limit lives on the component and the calendar reads it one hop",
  "plant:plant-wide": "a plant-total factor no single component owns (module count, housekeeping, aux cooling per MW, subsystem fraction)",
  "plant:exposure": "an EXPOSE or rollup sibling attribute that must stay a plant sibling for the aggregation producers",
  "plant:instance-own": "declared by the Stellaris instance itself for its own constraints and exposures"
 },
